MaskGuard's code and synthetic training data generator are original work, written for the TalentAP Mega Hackathon
2026 with Claude Code (Anthropic) as the coding assistant (see README, "AI usage"). No dataset is included in this
repository; the scripts in training/ download them.

The column classifier (src/maskguard/ml/pii_lgbm.txt.gz, version 2) was trained on MaskGuard's synthetic generator and
on columns derived from these datasets, which require attribution:
  - Nemotron-PII, NVIDIA (CC BY 4.0), https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/Nemotron-PII
  - Synthetic PII Finance Multilingual, Gretel (Apache-2.0),
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/gretelai/synthetic_pii_finance_multilingual
  - World Cities, GeoNames via github.com/datasets/world-cities (CC BY 4.0)
  - GDP, World Bank via github.com/datasets/gdp (CC BY 4.0)
  - other github.com/datasets packages under ODC-PDDL-1.0 (public domain), listed in training/realworld/sources.yaml

The web dashboard bundles IBM Plex Sans and Plex Mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1, src/maskguard/web/fonts/OFL.txt).
The external benchmark used for evaluation (bharat-pii-bench, Apache-2.0) is run separately and is not included.
